WEBVTT

00:00.740 --> 00:02.700
You've opened up a
shoe factory and you're

00:02.700 --> 00:06.020
trying to figure out how many
thousands of pairs of shoes

00:06.020 --> 00:08.980
to produce in order to
optimize your profit.

00:08.980 --> 00:13.505
And so let's let x equal the
thousands of pairs produced.

00:20.141 --> 00:21.640
Now let's think
about how much money

00:21.640 --> 00:22.990
you're going to make per pair.

00:22.990 --> 00:24.573
Actually, let me say
how much revenue,

00:24.573 --> 00:28.079
which is how much you actually
get to sell those shoes for.

00:28.079 --> 00:29.620
So let's write a
function right here.

00:29.620 --> 00:31.910
Revenue as a function of x.

00:31.910 --> 00:33.470
Well, you have a
wholesaler who's

00:33.470 --> 00:36.720
willing to pay you $10
per pair for as many pairs

00:36.720 --> 00:38.090
as you're willing to give him.

00:38.090 --> 00:42.100
So your revenue as a function
of x is going to be 10 times x.

00:42.100 --> 00:45.490
And since x is in thousands
of pairs produced, if x is 1,

00:45.490 --> 00:50.500
that means 1,000 pairs produced
times 10, which means $10,000.

00:50.500 --> 00:51.980
But this will just give you 10.

00:51.980 --> 00:54.350
So this right over here is
in thousands of dollars.

01:00.060 --> 01:02.570
So if x is 1, that means
1,000 pairs produced.

01:02.570 --> 01:05.260
10 times 1 says
r is equal to 10,

01:05.260 --> 01:09.689
but that really means $10,000.

01:09.689 --> 01:11.480
Now, it would be a nice
business if all you

01:11.480 --> 01:13.210
had was revenue and no costs.

01:13.210 --> 01:14.465
But you do have costs.

01:14.465 --> 01:16.590
You have materials, you
have to build your factory,

01:16.590 --> 01:18.089
have to pay your
employees, you have

01:18.089 --> 01:19.500
to pay the electricity bill.

01:19.500 --> 01:21.210
And so you hire a
bunch of consultants

01:21.210 --> 01:24.945
to come up with what your
cost is as a function of x.

01:28.170 --> 01:29.600
And they come up
with a function.

01:29.600 --> 01:33.270
They say it is the number of the
thousands of pairs you produce

01:33.270 --> 01:36.920
cubed minus 6 times the
thousands of pairs you produce

01:36.920 --> 01:41.950
squared plus 15 times
the thousands of pairs

01:41.950 --> 01:43.300
that you produce.

01:43.300 --> 01:46.580
And once again,
this is also going

01:46.580 --> 01:49.710
to be in thousands of dollars.

01:49.710 --> 01:54.682
Now, given these functions
of x for revenue and cost,

01:54.682 --> 01:58.930
what is profit as a
function of x going to be?

01:58.930 --> 02:03.580
Well, your profit
as a function of x

02:03.580 --> 02:07.710
is just going to be equal to
your revenue as a function of x

02:07.710 --> 02:09.800
minus your cost as
a function of x.

02:12.592 --> 02:14.300
If you produce a
certain amount and let's

02:14.300 --> 02:17.330
say you bring in, I don't
know, $10,000 of revenue

02:17.330 --> 02:19.970
and it costs you $5,000
to produce those shoes,

02:19.970 --> 02:21.529
you'll have $5,000 in profit.

02:21.529 --> 02:23.570
Those numbers aren't the
ones that would actually

02:23.570 --> 02:25.250
you would get from
this right here.

02:25.250 --> 02:27.230
I'm just giving you an example.

02:27.230 --> 02:28.990
So this is what you
want to optimize.

02:28.990 --> 02:36.170
You want to optimize
p as a function of x.

02:36.170 --> 02:37.140
So what is it?

02:37.140 --> 02:39.070
I've just said it here
in abstract terms,

02:39.070 --> 02:41.170
but we know what r of
x is and what's c of x.

02:41.170 --> 02:46.380
This is 10x minus
all of this business.

02:46.380 --> 02:53.590
So minus x to the third
plus 6x squared minus 15x.

02:53.590 --> 02:56.110
I just subtracted x
squared, you subtract

02:56.110 --> 02:58.880
6x squared it becomes positive,
you subtract a 15x it becomes

02:58.880 --> 03:03.520
negative 15x, and then we can
simplify this as-- let's see,

03:03.520 --> 03:07.200
we have negative x
to the third plus 6x

03:07.200 --> 03:12.370
squared minus 15x plus
10x, so that is minus 5x.

03:12.370 --> 03:16.497
Now if we want to optimize this
profit function analytically,

03:16.497 --> 03:18.080
the easiest way is
to think about what

03:18.080 --> 03:20.240
are the critical points
of this profit function

03:20.240 --> 03:21.740
and are any of those
critical points

03:21.740 --> 03:23.430
minimum points or
maximum points?

03:23.430 --> 03:26.870
And if one of them is a
maximum point, then we can say,

03:26.870 --> 03:28.190
well, let's produce that many.

03:28.190 --> 03:30.292
That is going to be--
we will have optimized

03:30.292 --> 03:32.500
or we will figure out the
quantity we need to produce

03:32.500 --> 03:35.020
in order to optimize our profit.

03:35.020 --> 03:36.710
So to figure out
critical points,

03:36.710 --> 03:39.600
we essentially have to find
the derivative of our function

03:39.600 --> 03:42.110
and figure out when does
that derivative equal 0

03:42.110 --> 03:44.070
or when is that
derivative undefined?

03:44.070 --> 03:46.490
That's the definition
of critical points.

03:46.490 --> 03:50.960
So p prime of x is going
to be equal to negative 3x

03:50.960 --> 03:55.790
squared plus 12x minus 5.

03:55.790 --> 03:58.100
And so this thing is going
to be defined for all x.

03:58.100 --> 04:00.140
So the only critical
points we're going to have

04:00.140 --> 04:04.280
is when the first derivative
right over here is equal to 0.

04:04.280 --> 04:10.470
So negative 3x squared plus 12x
minus 5 needs to be equal to 0

04:10.470 --> 04:12.190
in order for x to
be a critical point.

04:12.190 --> 04:14.300
So now we just have
to solve for x.

04:14.300 --> 04:17.829
And so we just are essentially
solving a quadratic equation.

04:17.829 --> 04:19.860
Just so that I don't
have as many negatives,

04:19.860 --> 04:21.820
let's multiply both
sides by negative 1.

04:21.820 --> 04:24.040
I just like to have a
clean first coefficient.

04:24.040 --> 04:25.950
So if we multiply both
sides by negative 1,

04:25.950 --> 04:33.330
we get 3x squared minus
12x plus 5 is equal to 0.

04:33.330 --> 04:36.700
And now we can use the quadratic
formula to solve for x.

04:36.700 --> 04:41.960
So x is going to be equal
to negative b, which is 12,

04:41.960 --> 04:43.910
plus or minus the square root.

04:43.910 --> 04:46.650
I always need to make my
radical signs wide enough.

04:46.650 --> 04:48.840
The square root of
b squared, which

04:48.840 --> 04:56.340
is 144, minus 4 times a, which
is 3, times c, which is 5.

04:59.340 --> 05:01.020
All of that over 2a.

05:01.020 --> 05:03.830
So 2 times 3 is 6.

05:03.830 --> 05:07.250
So x is equal to
12 plus or minus

05:07.250 --> 05:12.250
the square root of, let's see,
4 times 3 is 12 times 5 is 60.

05:12.250 --> 05:16.190
144 minus 60 is 84.

05:16.190 --> 05:17.990
All of that over 6.

05:17.990 --> 05:23.430
So x could be equal to 12 plus
the square root of 84 over 6

05:23.430 --> 05:29.930
or x could be equal to 12 minus
the square root of 84 over 6.

05:29.930 --> 05:31.580
So let's figure out
what these two are.

05:31.580 --> 05:34.270
And I'll use a calculator.

05:34.270 --> 05:37.140
I'll use the calculator
for this one.

05:37.140 --> 05:49.940
So I get, let's see, 12 plus the
square root of 84 divided by 6

05:49.940 --> 05:54.810
gives me 3.5--
I'll just say 3.53.

05:54.810 --> 05:59.440
So approximately
3.-- Actually, let me

05:59.440 --> 06:02.550
go one more digit, because
I'm talking about thousands.

06:02.550 --> 06:11.730
So let me say 3.528.

06:11.730 --> 06:15.050
So this would literally
be 3,528 shoes,

06:15.050 --> 06:19.170
because this is in
thousands, or pairs of shoes.

06:19.170 --> 06:21.370
And then let's do the
situation where we subtract.

06:21.370 --> 06:24.520
And actually we can look
at our previous entry

06:24.520 --> 06:27.220
and just change this
to a subtraction.

06:27.220 --> 06:30.570
Change that to not a
negative sign, a subtraction.

06:30.570 --> 06:31.530
There you go.

06:31.530 --> 06:37.470
And we get 0.4725.

06:37.470 --> 06:38.410
Let me remember that.

06:38.410 --> 06:41.810
0.4725.

06:41.810 --> 06:47.912
Approximately equal to 0.4725.

06:47.912 --> 06:49.370
I have a horrible
memory, so let me

06:49.370 --> 06:50.828
review that I wrote
the same thing.

06:50.828 --> 06:53.860
4725.

06:53.860 --> 06:54.360
Yep.

06:54.360 --> 06:55.470
All right.

06:55.470 --> 06:57.275
Now these are all
we know about these,

06:57.275 --> 06:58.710
or these are both
critical points.

06:58.710 --> 07:02.530
These are points at which
our derivative is equal to 0.

07:02.530 --> 07:04.680
But we don't know whether
they're minimum points,

07:04.680 --> 07:06.810
they're points at which
the function takes

07:06.810 --> 07:09.930
on a minimum value, a
maximum value, or neither.

07:09.930 --> 07:11.980
To do that, I'll use the
second derivative test

07:11.980 --> 07:14.210
to figure out if our
function is concave upwards

07:14.210 --> 07:17.750
or concave downwards or
neither at one of these points.

07:17.750 --> 07:20.630
So let's look at the
second derivative.

07:20.630 --> 07:24.530
So p prime prime
of x is going to be

07:24.530 --> 07:32.140
equal to negative 6x plus 12.

07:32.140 --> 07:37.440
And so if we look at-- let me
make sure I have enough space.

07:37.440 --> 07:44.660
So if we look at p
prime prime of 3.528.

07:44.660 --> 07:46.860
So let's see if I can
think this through.

07:46.860 --> 07:49.430
So this is between 3 and 4.

07:49.430 --> 07:52.700
So if we take the lower
value, 3 times negative 6

07:52.700 --> 07:56.180
is negative 18 plus 12 is
going to be less than 0.

07:56.180 --> 07:58.170
And if this was 4 it'd
be even more negative,

07:58.170 --> 07:59.878
so this thing is going
to be less than 0.

07:59.878 --> 08:02.301
Don't even have to use my
calculator to evaluate it.

08:02.301 --> 08:04.050
Now what about this
thing right over here?

08:04.050 --> 08:05.690
0.47.

08:05.690 --> 08:09.890
Well, 0.47, that's roughly 0.5.

08:09.890 --> 08:12.954
So negative 6 times
0.5 is negative 3.

08:12.954 --> 08:15.120
This is going to be nowhere
close to being negative.

08:15.120 --> 08:17.080
This is definitely
going to be positive.

08:17.080 --> 08:24.280
So p prime prime of
0.4725 is greater than 0.

08:24.280 --> 08:27.070
So the fact that the second
derivative is less than 0,

08:27.070 --> 08:31.850
that means that my
derivative is decreasing.

08:31.850 --> 08:33.840
My first derivative
is decreasing

08:33.840 --> 08:37.010
when x is equal to
this value, which

08:37.010 --> 08:39.830
means that our
graph, our function,

08:39.830 --> 08:41.590
is concave downwards here.

08:46.420 --> 08:50.650
And concave downwards means
it looks something like this.

08:50.650 --> 08:52.920
And so you can see what it
looks something like that,

08:52.920 --> 08:56.277
the slope is
constantly decreasing.

08:56.277 --> 08:58.610
So if you have an interval
where the slope is decreasing

08:58.610 --> 09:02.150
and you know the point where
the slope is exactly 0, which

09:02.150 --> 09:09.860
is where x is equal to
3.528, it must be a maximum.

09:09.860 --> 09:14.190
So we actually do take on a
maximum value when x is 3.528.

09:14.190 --> 09:17.124
On the other side we
see that over here we're

09:17.124 --> 09:17.790
concave upwards.

09:22.330 --> 09:24.751
The graph will look something
like this over here.

09:24.751 --> 09:27.000
And if the slope is 0 where
the graph looks like that,

09:27.000 --> 09:30.110
we see that that
is a local minimum.

09:33.199 --> 09:34.990
And so we definitely
don't want to do this.

09:34.990 --> 09:40.400
We would produce
472 and 1/2 units

09:40.400 --> 09:43.300
if we were looking to minimize
our profit, maximize our loss.

09:43.300 --> 09:45.672
So we definitely
don't want to do this.

09:45.672 --> 09:47.130
But let's actually
think about what

09:47.130 --> 09:49.600
our profit is going
to be if we produce

09:49.600 --> 09:55.480
3.528 thousands of
shoes, or 3,528 shoes.

09:55.480 --> 09:57.570
Well, to do that we just
have to input it back

09:57.570 --> 10:00.450
into our original profit
function right over here.

10:00.450 --> 10:01.780
So let's do that.

10:01.780 --> 10:04.160
So I get my calculator out.

10:04.160 --> 10:08.090
So my original profit
function is right over there.

10:08.090 --> 10:09.950
So I want to be able
to see that and that.

10:09.950 --> 10:24.570
So I get negative 3.528 to the
third power plus 6 times 3.528

10:24.570 --> 10:32.280
squared minus 5 times
3.528 gives me--

10:32.280 --> 10:39.990
and we get a drum roll now--
gives me a profit of 13.128.

10:39.990 --> 10:41.460
So let me write this down.

10:41.460 --> 10:48.570
The profit when I produce 3,528
shoes is approximately equal to

10:48.570 --> 10:51.860
or it is equal to, if I produce
exactly that many shoes,

10:51.860 --> 10:56.389
it's equal to 13.128.

10:56.389 --> 10:58.430
Or actually it's approximately,
because I'm still

10:58.430 --> 11:02.310
rounding 13.128.

11:02.310 --> 11:07.980
So if I produce 3,528
shoes in a given period,

11:07.980 --> 11:12.470
I'm going to have a
profit of $13,128.

11:12.470 --> 11:14.540
Remember, this right over
here is in thousands,

11:14.540 --> 11:17.590
this right over here
is 13.128 thousands

11:17.590 --> 11:21.850
of dollars in profit,
which is $13,128.

11:21.850 --> 11:25.811
Anyway, we are now going to
be rich shoe manufacturers.
